# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this plugin depends on, and that it is met.
#
# It is the first intake that carries text a stranger wrote into an
# agent. The agent cannot push (its clone has no remote and its home is
# an empty tmpfs; the kernel lands only what the checks pass), and since
# sandbox egress was bounded (docs/ROADMAP.md item 4) it cannot send the
# repository's contents, or the model token it runs with, anywhere it
# likes either: an attempt runs in a network namespace whose only route
# out is an allowlist proxy. The proxy lets through the model endpoint,
# always, and the hosts the target repository declares in its forge.toml:
#
#   [sandbox]
#   egress = ["registry.npmjs.org"]
#
# and refuses everything else. Forge quotes the issue body and tells the
# model it is data, which is a mitigation; the network policy is the
# boundary. `forge doctor` reports each project's policy (WARN when
# FORGE2_SANDBOX=0, which lifts it), and the built-in egress-probe
# operation asserts it from inside an attempt.
#
# Two things to know before enabling it:
#   - Keep the target repository's [sandbox] egress to the registries its
#     checks install from. Every host listed is a place a hostile issue
#     can send the repository's contents; a host that accepts uploads
#     (a paste site, an object store) does not belong there.
#   - The model token is still the operator's, not scoped to the task
#     (docs/GTM.md item 1). It can now reach only the model endpoint.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copy this file to "config" next to plugin.toml (or into the installed
# copy under FORGE2_HOME/plugins/github-issues/) and fill it in. It is
# shell, sourced by github-issues.sh: KEY=value lines, one per line.

# owner/name of the GitHub repository to watch. Required.
GH_REPO=owner/name

# Only open issues carrying this label are filed as tasks.
LABEL=forge

# Added to the issue when its task lands. Unset (the default) skips
# labeling.
#DONE_LABEL=forge-done

# How often to check GH_REPO for new issues, in seconds. Never less than
# 30, regardless of what is set here.
POLL_SECONDS=120

# Local path to the git repository new tasks are queued against.
# Required.
TARGET_REPO=/path/to/repo

# The workflow new tasks run (see `forge workflows`).
WORKFLOW=direct
